    "title": "Seven Homes, One Neck",
    "summary": "All seven modes on this root live inside the same five windows, and what actually separates them is one decision about home and one note leaned against it.",
    "tags": ["modes", "fretboard", "ear", "theory"],
    "readingTimeMin": 4,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-15"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every one of the seven modes in this pathway happened inside the same five windows, on the same root, using hand positions two other pathways already put in your fingers. "
        },
        {
          "text": "One Map, Any Key",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "caged-the-whole-neck"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "What the Third Was Worth",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-what-the-third-was-worth"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " are where those two pathways ended. This is where all three of them meet."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Here it is twice, frets 4 to 8, the E form — first filled with the brightest of the seven, then with the darkest."
        }
      ]
    },
