        "root": "A",
        "form": "E",
        "scale": "lydian",
        "caption": "The bright end of the ladder — no note in this box asks to be avoided over the chord it's built on"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "live",
      "component": "caged-shape",
      "props": {
        "root": "A",
        "form": "E",
        "scale": "locrian",
        "caption": "The dark end, the same five frets — the chord underneath still won't hold"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Both boxes draw every note in the window, not a grip a hand would hold at once — true of every one of these diagrams this pathway has shown you, and easy to forget staring at a fretboard full of dots. What matters here isn't how many of them there are. It's that the frame holding them — same form, same frets, same root — never moved once to get from the brightest mode to the darkest, even though almost every degree inside it did."
        }
      ]
